From: Pratik Vishwakarma <Pratik.Vishwakarma@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 05:54:59 +0000
Subject: x86/CPU/AMD: Carve out a Zen5 models range
Git-commit: 52075128273ace53e6254e37899a47d40d4baf45
Patch-mainline: v7.2-rc6
References: bsc#1287771 CVE-2024-21963

Family 0x1a, model 0xd0..0xd7 belongs to the Zen5 generation. Carve it
out from the larger, Zen6 range where former doesn't belong.

  [ bp: Rewrite commit message, add tags. ]

Fixes: b5f53e6d3d32 ("x86/CPU/AMD: Add more Zen6 models")
Signed-off-by: Pratik Vishwakarma <Pratik.Vishwakarma@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Borislav Petkov (AMD) <bp@alien8.de>
Cc: <stable@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260729055459.15904-1-Pratik.Vishwakarma@amd.com

Acked-by: Nikolay Borisov <nik.borisov@suse.com>
---
 arch/x86/kernel/cpu/amd.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/amd.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/amd.c
@@ -625,11 +625,13 @@ static void bsp_init_amd(struct cpuinfo_
 	case 0x1a:
 		switch (c->x86_model) {
 		case 0x00 ... 0x2f:
+		case 0xd0 ... 0xd7:
 			setup_force_cpu_cap(X86_FEATURE_ZEN5);
 			break;
 		case 0x50 ... 0x5f:
 		case 0x80 ... 0xaf:
 		case 0xc0 ... 0xcf:
+		case 0xd8 ... 0xef:
 			setup_force_cpu_cap(X86_FEATURE_ZEN6);
 			break;
 		default:
